# The pointer contract's code hash: base58(BLAKE3(pointer-v1.wasm)).
#
# This value is the root of the whole convention. Every pointer key in the
# ecosystem is BLAKE3(this || that pointer's params), so if this changes, every
# published pointer re-keys and every consumer resolving through one is
# stranded -- with no pointer left to point at the pointer.
#
# It is enforced by CI (`./build-wasm.sh --check`). Changing it is a flag day.
